# Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the React + Vite project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (latest version)
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json with the new dependency

### 2. Component Integration
**Modified: `src/main.tsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/react";`
- Integrated the `<SpeedInsights />` component in the root application render tree
- Placed the component inside the `QueryClientProvider` to ensure it tracks metrics across the entire application

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), the SpeedInsights component was added to the main application entry point. This ensures that Speed Insights will:
- Track Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS)
- Monitor page load performance
- Collect real user metrics (RUM)
- Report data to the Vercel dashboard when deployed

## Framework-Specific Configuration

This project uses React 19.2.0 with Vite 8.0.16. The React-specific integration was used (`@vercel/speed-insights/react`), which is optimized for React applications and provides automatic metric collection without additional configuration.

## Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ No TypeScript errors
- ✅ Package lock file updated
- ✅ Component properly integrated in render tree

## Next Steps

Once this is deployed to Vercel:
1. The Speed Insights data will automatically start being collected
2. View metrics in the Vercel Dashboard under the "Speed Insights" tab
3. No additional configuration is required for basic functionality

## Notes

- The SpeedInsights component is lightweight and will not impact application performance
- It only collects metrics in production; minimal overhead in development
- The component is placed after the router and dev tools to ensure proper tracking of all routes
